rem Digit Factorial Chains
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=74
rem Count starts below a limit with a
rem sixty-term digit factorial chain

use sequences
use graph
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 1000000
option Terms integer = 60

rem f(n) = f(n // 10) + Fact(n mod 10).
rem Extend by digit length so every
rem prefix is already in the table.
Fact = array shape 10
  1 1 2 6 24 120 720 5040 40320 362880
end
rem Six-digit starts reach 6 * 9!;
rem 1999999 reaches one more. This
rem bound is closed under successors.
Bound = (Limit - 1) 2177281 max
Next = array 0
for Top in 10 ** (1 to 7) - 1
  V = (Next len) to (Top Bound min) array
  More = Next (V // 10) + Fact (V mod 10)
  Next = concat Next More copy
end
Next = Next (1 to Bound)

rem Chains are paths of the successor
rem graph; lengths counts terms.
Lens = Next functional lengths
Short = Lens take (Limit - 1)
Answer = Short equal Terms count
Answer print
